      "comments": 182,
      "author": "shmulc",
      "published": "2026-11-07T20:45:32Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Anthropic's Claude Code CLI persistent approval setting inadvertently led developers to commit credentials and secrets to public GitHub repositories.",
        "At least 1,122 public files leaked sensitive passwords after users bypassed command execution confirmations via the 'Don't Ask Again' prompt.",
        "AI coding agents require robust default .gitignore rules and automated secret scanning before granting unattended write or commit privileges."
      ]
