      "author": "novedevo",
      "published": "2026-11-07T21:05:35Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Persistent memory safety flaws like buffer overflows and use-after-free continue driving mandates to replace legacy C with safe alternatives like Rust.",
        "Total deprecation of C remains stalled by entrenched kernel dependencies, stable ABI requirements, mature toolchains, and prohibitive codebase rewrite costs.",
        "Pragmatic defense requires adopting Rust for exposed attack surfaces while enforcing hardware-assisted CFI, sanitizers, and strict compiler hardening on legacy C."
      ]
